WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.830
<i>Previously on </i>Zombie Land Saga Revenge<i>...</i>

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.810
<i>It's been a few months since we bombed at 
EFS as hard as any idol group ever has,</i>

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.060
<i>and things are starting to look 
up a bit for Franchouchou!</i>

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.410
<i>Everyone is feeling a lot more motivated,</i>

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.190
<i>and Lily-chan even went on a
talent TV show on her own!</i>

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.570
<i>Her magical power got her to the finals,</i>

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.520
<i>but then she was up against 
a child acting prodigy!</i>

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.240
<i>And they were set to sing the same song?!</i>

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.580
<i>That's some band-standingly, 
soul-strainingly bad news!</i>

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.480
<i>But our Lily-chan was able to whip up
 a bold, improvised scat arrangement!</i>

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.010
<i>It was so seriously magical 
that it had everyone</i>

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.010
<i>going shoobieshoobie deeba daba beba bop!</i>

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.460
You look like you're 
racking your brain again.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.290
In another five years, you're 
gonna have the same look.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.200
I saw the chatter online, too.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.380
About the resemblance to Lily Hoshikawa.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.700
More people are noticing Number Three 
and Four's resemblances, too.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.220
Well, they're better known than ever thanks 
to that radio show and the Iron Frill business.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.300
Most people are just making fun of them 
for being a collection of lookalikes.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.900
I guess that comes with the territory 
when you're trying to get famous.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.480
You were the first one to notice 
Number Four looking like Junko Konno.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.890
You should've started 
writing stuff right away.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.990
I don't wanna write a bunch 
of diet speculation.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.100
Well, the only theory that makes sense

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.510
is that their producer is collecting 
a bunch of lookalikes.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.340
I bet the other girls probably 
look like somebody, too.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.280
Only other explanation is that they
were revived, like a bunch of zombies.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.890
If you're serious, maybe you wanna 
go write for that occult mag <i>Mu</i>.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.500
I'll head there for an interview right now!

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.940
Not! I'm actually going to lunch.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.780
The other girls, huh...?

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.290
Even if we have nothing else, 
we still have the future.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.200
A lowest point? Starting over from 
zero? That's just part of the saga.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.940
Even if we burn out in the 
process, we'll make it come true!

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.310
This is where our revenge begins!

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:53.380
<b>{title}Zombie Land Saga 
Revenge</b>

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.680
<b>Walking Bet SAGA</b>

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.250
Peek...

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.300
G'morning!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.180
Good morning.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.210
Morning.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:26.280
Well, ladies of Franchouchou, 
how have you been?

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.180
Looks like you're getting 
back in the swing of things.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.270
Hardly. We need to aim 
higher than ever before.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.070
Very good. I like that spunk, Ai!

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:37.940
Seems like folks outside of Saga 
are hearing about us more.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.930
I bet we can blast on to 
getting our revenge for EFS.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.550
Yes, exactly, Saki!

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.740
Let's keep trying all kinds of new things!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.750
All right, then! Let's get 
down to a strategy meeting...

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.370
except we can't do that, 
can we, you airheaded zombies?!

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:55.680
We've still got almost 20 
million yen in debt, dumbass!

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.370
How are we supposed to do any damn 
thing without any damn money?!

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.880
This ain't some story where we learn
how to enjoy life despite being broke!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.310
You were only able to do the 
radio show and the opening act gig

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.220
and that audition show because 
they don't cost jack!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.420
Until we get liquid, there's 
not gonna be any challenges

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.020
or revenges or anything else,
 you ninnyhammers!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.970
The debt is your fault in the first place!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:13.680
Quit acting like a kid!

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.770
Okay! So, that being the case, why don't 
we all get out there and get that bread?!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.690
That goes for you, too!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.170
Tae-chan has today off so she can rest!

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.940
Nobody ever earned by sleeping!

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:33.030
Without money, you won't be able to have 
your fun little family dinners anymore!

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.130
Sakura-san...

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.190
Please, don't think of 
yourself as a ninnyhammer.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.010
O-Okay?

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.500
Have a good day!

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.590
We're heading out!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:49.720
<b>Yamada</b>

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:50.710
There.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.210
Here's today's list.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.130
Are you going to be all right?

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.420
Be careful out there, you hear?

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.280
Romero-han, look after her.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.860
<i>I love taking detours! (Love them!)</i>

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:22.170
<i>Nothing beats the slow path! (So much fun!)</i>

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:27.760
<i>But you can't forget to get 
those errands done, too!</i>

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.710
<i>Onions and pork ribs! (Ribs of pork!)</i>

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:33.690
<i>Carrots and potatoes! (Potatoes!)</i>

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:41.130
<i>Curry for dinner tonight, 
yeah, yeah, yeah! I love it!</i>

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:48.700
I talked a big game, but big stories in Saga?

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.910
Not like I'm in Tokyo anymore...

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.570
That's Number Zero.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.040
<i>Franchouchou's Number Zero...</i>

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.980
<i>Even in that group, she stands out.</i>

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.280
<i>She doesn't sing, for one thing.</i>

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.950
<i>And when she dances, she's 
basically doing her own thing.</i>

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.990
<i>She has these strange bursts of 
activity that are almost childlike.</i>

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.810
<i>But none of the other members 
seem to think that's strange,</i>

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.460
<i>and instead of getting upset, 
they almost seem to love her for it.</i>

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.230
<i>Among fans, her devil-may-care, 
free-wheeling,</i>

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.410
<b>Number Zero had the strongest presence in the
 Drive-In Tori commercial #NumberZero #Franchouchou</b>

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.410
<b> Momentum is Number Zero's whole appeal! Cock-a-doodle-doo!</b>

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.910
<b>I get anxious seeing Franchouchou without their mascot, 
Number Zero #NumberZero #Franchouchou</b>

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.910
<b>I'd love to see what Number Zero has to offer outside of Drive-In Tori's rooster.
 I bet she could do the siren they play during Koshien.</b>

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.410
<b>It's amazing how Number Zero always nails it during the big numbers for the dances</b>

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.410
<b>She's too wild lol Number Zero FTW lol</b>

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.260
<i>mysterious behavior has 
earned a lot of love.</i>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.250
<b>Number Zero's 
godlike cuteness!!!!</b>

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:44.780
You can definitely say she's got a certain 
something the rest of the group doesn't...

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.930
Oh, Zero-chan, are you out shopping?

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.490
I saw Number Six on TV the other day!

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.840
That little dear is really something.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:00.230
I just bought some fish 
croquettes. Have one!

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:04.450
Now, don't go eating the bag like last time.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.320
Sure, something for Rome-chan, too.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.850
Number Zero, Number Zero! Whatcha up to?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.110
Oh, you're shopping today?

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:20.380
You can have some Irohanihohoho then.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.630
She fits right in...

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.220
Is this a shortcut?

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.070
<i>She's eating it?!</i>

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:49.720
<i>So fast!</i>

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.780
Haven't done this kinda thing in a while...

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.800
<b>Minamoto
 Family Grave</b>

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.800
<b>Yamada Family
 Ancestral Grave</b>

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.550
<b>Super Market
 Morinaga Karatsu Store</b>

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:20.970
Welcome!

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.900
Oh, it's you today, Number Zero?

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.830
I finally saved up enough money for Mama—

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.730
er, my mom, so I can buy her a scooter

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.600
to replace the bike that exploded.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.070
To be honest, we're going through 
a bit of a rebranding with our team.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:44.140
Check this out... now it's
Dance Team Dorami!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.000
<b>Dance Team Dorami</b>

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.510
You could act a little surprised.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.310
<b>Thinly-sliced Bacon (Canadian)</b>

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:50.310
As for why we went with dance,

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:53.380
after seeing Number Two at 
Franchouchou's performances,

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.090
I figure there's more than 
one way to tear it up.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.680
So we held a rally with all members 
and decided to go into dance.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.660
There's also the fact Mama— er,

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.420
Mom will probably worry less this way.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.350
Man, I always end up talking 
your ear off for some reason.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.930
How much of that did you hear?!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.240
Instant Foods
Curry
Spices
Sauces

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.060
Anyway, the idea is that one 
day we're gonna get big

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:20.470
and be on the same stage as Franchouchou!

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:21.200
Count on it!

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.820
<i>That's a sweet story.</i>

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:27.970
<i>She's chewing on her?!</i>

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:30.890
Aw, I keep telling you that hurts!

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:31.940
Maria-chan.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.340
Is she chewing on your buns again?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.000
We're here to pick you up.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:38.280
Oh, it's already time?

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:38.990
Oof, that hurts!

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:42.440
Number Zero, we're about to head to 656 Plaza

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:46.840
for the Hisanaka Pharmaceuticals 
Dance Battle 2019, ow, ow, ow...

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.210
which we're entered in.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.200
You wanna come check it out?

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:55.720
Our next judge is one of the people who 
helped make this tournament possible.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.600
You all know her from Saganship Z,

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.360
the public relations manager 
from Hisanaka Pharmaceuticals!

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.610
If you're worn out from dancing, 
by all means, try out our products.

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:05.450
Let's get out there and do this!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.370
We'll do our best!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.470
What she said!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.060
<b>Bird</b>

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:19.210
And there he is! 
Our five-time grand champion!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:22.620
Representing Saga, it's Cocco-kun!

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:51.140
What a surprise we have, folks!

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.010
It's Number Zero from Franchouchou!

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:55.990
She's on stage?!

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:56.890
Seriously?!

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:01.880
Unfortunately, I'm afraid there is no 
last-minute entry for this competition!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.560
And that's our grand champion for you!

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.780
He's happy to take on the challenge!

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:44.580
That's... gotta be so fast it doesn't 
look like she's moving... right?

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.740
And Cocco-kun is down!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:06.910
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:11.930
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:15.450
Number Zero! I can't believe you won 
the whole thing by doing a run-in!

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.930
<b>Bonus Prize
 10 KG of onions</b>

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.930
<b>Grand Prize 
30,000 yen</b>

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.640
And what was up with that spinning?!

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:18.320
It looked like your head 
wasn't even spinning!

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:20.410
Seriously, it seemed almost impossible!

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.180
What a flex!

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.250
You even got the prize money, too!

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.910
I bet Number Two and the rest of the 
group will be thrilled to hear about it!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:32.640
Whoa, whoa, whoa! What are you doing?! 
You've gotta take it!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.340
I can't take it!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.270
Just give me those onions instead.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:40.630
Why?!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.950
What's all this? Is it a stickup?

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.510
Are we looking at some iddy-biddy 
baby muggers out here today?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:49.620
I was just trying to give 
her this money back,

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.960
but she's acting like she doesn't 
want it, or doesn't care...

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.750
You mean to tell me you don't 
know what to do with some cash?

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:56.770
Y-Yeah, I guess...

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.920
Leave it to me!

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:02.230
It will be this officer's pleasure to 
show you how to put it to good use!

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.480
<b>Karatsu</b>

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:09.150
Should a cop really be taking 
us to a place like this?

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:13.200
It's my duty as a Saga policeman to aid 
and assist the prefecture's citizens!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:20.330
<b>Karatsu</b>

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:20.340
Seriously, Saga...?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.910
Maria-chan, it's Korosuke!

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.710
Bummer city....

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:35.340
Y-You girls better get along, 
or I'll bring you in!

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:39.410
We're not gonna do anything.
 We can't make trouble right now.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.100
Sounding kinda weak there.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:44.130
Hey, dumbass! It's because 
Misa-san is racing today!

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:45.370
Misa...

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:49.040
Yeah, since you guys stopped being 
bikers, you might not have heard...

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.650
But after that game of chicken,

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:57.100
Misa-san has been chasing after the kind of 
ultimate speed that Number Two showed off

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.640
by getting into boat racing.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.680
I guess she found a new 
way to tear it up, too...

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:10.030
But she hasn't won even once...

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:12.270
Misa the Fallen Angel!

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:15.440
She always ends up accelerating 
at the wrong time and wiping out...

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:19.830
The people who were calling her 
the runaway princess at first

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.440
make jokes now about betting 
on her being a bust!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:25.980
They're even calling her Misa the Warthog!

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.360
Here's hoping you can make 
a turn for a change.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:38.210
That's just sad...

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.780
You wanna die?!

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:44.690
If she screws up like that in front of me,
 I'll kill her myself.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:49.510
All right, let's move along. 
We've got another race to bet on.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:52.420
Here.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.760
If you make a bit extra, 
cut me in on it, okay?

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:58.600
<b>Calling...
 Chief</b>

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.820
Yes, hello, over!

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:06.380
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:12.110
Uh, well, I'm, uh, upholding 
my duty... as Saga PD...

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.530
<i>Is it the horse track?</i>

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:19.960
It's... not the horse track, no.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:20.860
Over.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.590
<i>She's sucking on it!</i>

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:30.960
I must be exhausted...

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:35.420
Franchouchou!

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:40.460
I swear to you... I'm not 
at the horse track, over.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.520
<b>Ticket Out</b>

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.150
<b>Ticket Out</b>

00:16:55.490 --> 00:17:00.190
Sure, I love horses! I'm just... 
not at the horse track.

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:00.970
Over.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.150
Number Zero!

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:07.440
We're over here!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.260
Misa's race is coming up...

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:19.220
Now then, I wonder how that 
gal's gonna do today?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.340
I do like the way she races, but...

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:28.100
Maria?!

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:50.140
You've got this, Misa-san!

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:53.140
There you go! That's it! Nice racing!

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:14.120
<i>Watch this, Maria...</i>

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.510
<i>And watch close!</i>

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.660
<i>Number Two...</i>

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.650
<i>Check this out!</i>

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:35.350
She did it!

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.350
Too sweet!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.770
That was the eel goby turn!

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:41.590
She pulled off the legendary technique...

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:44.920
That was it... It truly was the eel goby!

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:48.250
The eel goby has returned to Karatsu!

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.820
That was a hell of a race. 
I couldn't resist watching it.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:08.330
This might not be the horse track, 
but that was an awesome race!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.950
Should've bet on it...

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:21.060
What bet did you make, Number Zero?

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.010
Huh?

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.400
Seriously...?

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:55.510
I ended up following her all day...

00:19:55.510 --> 00:20:00.560
and now I only have more questions, 
with no answers to show for it.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:01.500
I'm done.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:04.940
Tae-cha—

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.800
Hey, Maria!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:10.370
You were late, so we were 
worried! What happened?

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:19.950
Nicely done, Tae-han.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.070
It's good to see you again, Number Two!

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:25.180
Yeah! What brings you by?

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.670
Well, I ran into Number 
Zero at the supermarket,

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:30.060
and man, a whole hell of a lot happened!

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.070
Check this out...

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:38.140
She won big at the boat 
races! That's 20 million.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.630
Did Number Zero seriously win all this?!

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.290
20 million... How much is that?!

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:46.370
Hey, shrimpy, how much is 
20 million, seriously?!

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:47.540
Wh-Wh-What do we do, what do we do?!

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:50.610
If Number Zero really did win all this...

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:52.610
Can't we pay back our debt?

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:55.940
Ta-Ta-Ta— er, N-Number Zero, 
let's tell Kotaro-san!

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:05.790
Number Two...

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:15.570
Let's gracefully accept.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.400
All right!

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:20.260
That turned out to be quite the errand run.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:24.570
Damn, Tae's way more useful than Shades!

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:25.900
You're amazing, Tae-chan!

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.630
Thank you so much, Tae-chan!

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:06.060
I'm done.

00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:10.880
You were late, so we were 
worried! What happened?

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:15.030
Ta-Ta-Ta— er, N-Number Zero, 
let's tell Kotaro-san!

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:23.700
Only other explanation is that they
were revived, like a bunch of zombies.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:25.670
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:26.900
Sakura here!

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:29.280
You can never tell what'll happen, huh?

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:31.240
Becoming a zombie was definitely like that.

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:35.430
Next time on <i>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</i> 
Episode 7: "Mai Mai Revolution SAGA."

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Episode 7: Mai Mai Revolution SAGA</b>

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:38.150
You can never tell what'll happen!
